To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. Create a new HTML document and save it as `image_with_caption.html`.
2. Add the following code inside the `<head>` section to define some styles for our page:

```css
#img-container {
  text-align: center;
}

#img-container img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

#img-container p {
  margin: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}
```

3. Inside the `<body>` section, add a `<div>` element with the ID of `img-container`. This will be used to center our image and caption.

```html
<div id="img-container">

</div>
```

4. Inside the `img-container` div, we'll add our image and caption. We want to make the image into a link, so wrap it inside an anchor tag (`<a>`) with the URL where you want the user to go when they click on the image.

```html
<a href="http://www.example.com">
  <img src="image.jpg" alt="Image">
</a>

<p>Caption goes here</p>
```

5. Save your file and open it in a browser. You should now see your image with the caption centered below it. When you click on the image, you'll be taken to the URL you provided in the anchor tag.

