```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function ($a, $b) use ($order) {
        $ageA = $a['age'];
        $ageB = $b['age'];
        if ($ageA === $ageB) {
            return 0; // If ages are equal, don't change order
        }
        return $order === 'ASC' ? $ageA < $ageB : $ageA > $ageB; // Switch based on order parameter
    });
    return $set;
}
```

This implementation uses a closure as the comparison callback for `usort()`, allowing us to easily access the `$order` parameter and compare the ages of each element in the desired order. The function returns the sorted array after calling `usort()`.

